.TH OMORFOS\-RULES 5 "" omorfos "omorfos manual"
.nh
.ad l
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
omorfos\-rules \- rules.yaml, how the omorfos desktop treats particular windows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/omorfos/rules.yaml\fR, usually \fB~/.config/omorfos/rules.yaml\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Rules for particular windows, by the program they are of or their title: the workspace they open on, whether they open maximized, fullscreen, shaded, kept above or on every workspace, with or without a frame, and whether they are private, veiled in pictures of the screen.
.PP
It is read again as soon as it is saved. If it has a mistake, its contents before are kept, and the mistake is shown among the notifications and printed by \fBomorfosctl config check\fR, with its line and column; the other files still apply.
.SH KEYS
.TP
\fBrules\fR
Rules applied to new windows. Every matching rule applies, in order, so a later rule overrides an earlier one.
.TP
\fBrules[].above\fR
Open the window kept above those that are not, or not.
.TP
\fBrules[].decorations\fR
Draw a titlebar and border around the window, or not.
.TP
\fBrules[].fullscreen\fR
Open the window fullscreen, or not.
.TP
\fBrules[].match\fR
Which windows the rule applies to.
.TP
\fBrules[].match.app_id\fR
Pattern for the application identifier, such as \fBfirefox\fR or \fBorg.gnome.*\fR. \fB*\fR stands for any run of characters.
.TP
\fBrules[].match.title\fR
Pattern for the window title. \fB*\fR stands for any run of characters.
.TP
\fBrules[].maximized\fR
Open the window maximized, or not.
.TP
\fBrules[].private\fR
Hide the window in any picture taken of the screen, or not: blank, or blurred. Unlike the others this holds for as long as the window matches, not only when it opens: a title that comes to match hides it.
.RS
.TP
\fBblank\fR
.TP
\fBblur\fR
.RE
.TP
\fBrules[].shaded\fR
Open the window rolled up into its titlebar, or not. A window without a titlebar is not rolled up.
.TP
\fBrules[].sticky\fR
Open the window on every workspace of its screen, or not.
.TP
\fBrules[].workspace\fR
Open the window on the workspace with this number. From 1 to 32.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
rules:
  \- match: { app_id: firefox }
    workspace: 1
  \- match: { app_id: "org.gnome.*", title: "*Preferences" }
    maximized: false
    decorations: true
  \- match: { app_id: mpv }
    fullscreen: true
  \- match: { title: "*Bank*" }
    private: true
  \- match: { app_id: org.gnome.Loupe }
    private: blur
  \- match: { app_id: "*notes*" }
    above: true
    sticky: true
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBomorfos\fR(1), \fBomorfosctl\fR(1), \fBomorfos\-config\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-keys\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-menu\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-theme\fR(5)
